{
  "_what": "Where each nail is in Em's product photographs, for tools/cut-ems-nails.py. Em makes hand-painted press-on nails and sells them as Ems Nails 4 You; Stimpunks gave her a creator grant for the photography equipment these were taken with, and she gave us permission to use her photographs on Stimpunks.World however we like. That is permission to use, not a licence to pass on: the photographs and every strip cut from them are excluded from CC BY-SA in LICENSE.",
  "_boxes": "Each box is [left, top, right, bottom] in the 1200px photograph as her site serves it, drawn round one nail by eye on a grid. A box only has to hold its nail and as little of the stand under it as possible: the cutting is Apple's subject lifting, run on this Mac, so nothing is sent anywhere.",
  "_turn": "up means the nail's free edge is already at the top of the photograph. down means it points down and is turned over. auto means the nail lies some other way (a close-up) and the narrower end is taken to be the tip.",
